Reason: The provided `CompletableTimer` class is a thin wrapper that delegates the actual work to an external `Scheduler`. Its behavior and performance are dominated by the scheduler implementation and system timing, not by any computational logic within the class itself. Consequently, a microbenchmark using JMH would primarily measure scheduler overhead and timing inaccuracies rather than the intrinsic performance characteristics of this code, making a dedicated JMH benchmark unnecessary.